  "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{2}{3}$ on the left and $\\frac{2}{12}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133144/assets/6f6687c4190a54e9974dc600ced3a2662718cce1bcd5d49410a994259ac06e58.png)\n\nThe division operation splits each vertical line into $4$ equal parts. So the shaded parts on the left are $4$ times larger than the shaded parts on the right. \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}÷4=\\frac{2}{12}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $4.$",
